Feature: Voice-Guided Transaction Review
  As an attorney (or donor) reviewing flagged transactions
  I want to ask about a flag by voice and hear the explanation narrated back
  So that I can understand the donor's concerns hands-free, while the audio never leaves our infrastructure

  Background:
    Given the donor has flagged transactions from applying their LPA rules

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  # GROUP A: Key Examples
  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

  # Why: The headline "talk me through this" path — the spoken question is transcribed, answered, and the answer is spoken back (ADR-POC-015 cascade)
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=high] ASSUM-008 — outbound narration is a binary audio stream the browser plays directly
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: An attorney asks to be talked through a single flag by voice
    Given I am an attorney with an active relationship to the donor
    And the donor has a flagged transaction
    When I ask the platform to talk me through that flag by voice
    Then my spoken question should be transcribed to text
    And I should receive a spoken narration explaining the flag
    And the narration should play back in my browser

  # Why: Core ADR-POC-015 invariant — voice is I/O only; reasoning stays in text and is reused, no second model forms a new judgement
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: The narration reuses the explanation already recorded for the flag
    Given a flagged transaction whose flag already explains why it was raised
    When I ask the platform to talk me through that flag by voice
    Then the narration should convey the same explanation already recorded for that flag
    And no new judgement about the transaction should be formed for the narration

  # Why: Whole-batch narration is a fire-and-forget background task per ADR-POC-015 Decision 6
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=high] ASSUM-013 — single-transaction narration runs inline; whole-batch narration runs in the background
  @key-example
  Scenario: An attorney asks to be talked through all of a donor's flags
    Given I am an attorney with an active relationship to the donor
    And the donor has several flagged transactions
    When I ask the platform to talk me through all of the flags by voice
    Then the narration request should be accepted and prepared in the background
    And I should be able to follow it until the narration is ready

  # Why: The inbound query response carries the transcript and the action taken (ADR-POC-015 transcript + action shape, in domain terms)
  @key-example
  Scenario: A voice query reports what was understood and what was done
    Given I am an attorney with an active relationship to the donor
    When I ask a question by voice about the donor's flags
    Then I should be told what the platform understood me to say
    And I should be told what action it took in response

  # Why: The flagged-transaction view is shared by donors too; a donor can narrate their own flags
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=medium] ASSUM-007 — donors can narrate their own flags, not only attorneys
  @key-example
  Scenario: A donor asks to be talked through their own flag by voice
    Given I am the donor signed in to my own account
    And I have a flagged transaction
    When I ask the platform to talk me through that flag by voice
    Then I should receive a spoken narration explaining the flag

  # Why: The audit trail is the FCA narrative — the interaction is logged with transcript text, actor and transaction, but never the raw audio (ADR-POC-015 Decision 5)
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=high] ASSUM-011 — the audit log keeps the transcript, actor and referenced transactions, never the raw audio
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: A voice interaction is recorded in the audit log without the recording
    Given I am an attorney with an active relationship to the donor
    When I ask the platform to talk me through a flag by voice
    Then the voice interaction should appear in the donor's audit log
    And the record should name me as the actor and the transaction I asked about
    And the record should include what I said as text but never the recorded audio

  # Why: ADR-POC-014 — the query outcome is content-negotiated (structured data for any client, page fragment for HTMX); narration audio is the separate stream exception
  @key-example
  Scenario: A voice query outcome is served both as structured data and as a page fragment
    Given I am an attorney with an active relationship to the donor
    When I submit a voice question and request the outcome as structured data and again as a page fragment
    Then both responses should report the same transcript, the same action taken, and the same narration to play

