  # Why: ADR-POC-015 Decision 2 — voice is additive and optional; when a voice service is down the feature degrades to the text UI, never a hard dependency
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=high] ASSUM-012 — when voice is unavailable the feature degrades to the text UI; there is no cloud failover
  @edge-case @smoke
  Scenario: Voice review degrades to the text view when the voice service is unavailable
    Given the local voice service is unavailable
    When I open the flagged-transaction view and try to use voice
    Then the flags should still be fully readable as text
    And I should be told that spoken narration is unavailable right now

  # Why: Cache is keyed by the rules in force — after a rules correction the narration must reflect the new rules, not the cached old one
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=high] ASSUM-005 — the narration cache is keyed by the transaction and the rules in force
  @edge-case
  Scenario: Re-narration after the rules change reflects the corrected rules
    Given I previously heard the narration for a flag
    When the donor's rules are corrected and I ask to hear that flag's narration again
    Then the narration should reflect the corrected rules
    And it should not replay the narration from before the correction

  # Why: Nothing to narrate is a clean outcome, not an error, and must not fabricate a concern
  @edge-case
  Scenario: Asking to be talked through a transaction that has no flag reports nothing of concern
    Given a transaction that carries no flag
    When I ask the platform to talk me through that transaction by voice
    Then I should be told there is nothing of concern to narrate
    And no flag should be invented for that transaction

  # Why: Donors double-tap; concurrent identical narration requests must not double-synthesise the same audio
  @edge-case
  Scenario: Concurrent identical narration requests produce a single synthesis
    Given no narration has yet been produced for a flag
    When I ask to hear that flag's narration twice at the same instant
    Then the narration should be produced only once
    And both requests should receive the same narration

  # Why: Whole-batch narration is multi-pass; a failure partway must keep the narrations already produced
  @edge-case
  Scenario: A batch narration that fails partway keeps the narrations already produced
    Given a whole-batch narration is being prepared across several flags
    When one flag's narration fails after earlier ones have succeeded
    Then the narrations already produced should remain available
    And I should be told the narration did not complete in full

