  # GROUP G: Expansion — Integration Boundaries
  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

  # Why: Partial degradation — when synthesis is down but transcription is up, the text answer must still come through (ADR-POC-015 cascade legs are independent)
  @edge-case
  Scenario: When spoken narration is unavailable the transcript and text explanation are still delivered
    Given the platform can transcribe my question but cannot produce spoken narration
    When I ask to be talked through a flag by voice
    Then I should still be told what the platform understood me to say
    And I should still see the explanation of the flag as text
    And I should be told that spoken narration is unavailable right now

  # Why: Narration reuses already-recorded reasoning — it must not depend on the reasoning model being free (ADR-POC-015: narration text comes from the existing FEAT-POC-004 path)
  @edge-case
  Scenario: Narrating an existing flag does not depend on the reasoning model being free
    Given a flag whose explanation has already been recorded
    And the reasoning model is currently busy
    When I ask to be talked through that flag by voice
    Then the narration should still be produced from the recorded explanation
    And it should not wait on the reasoning model
